Space Map - Instructions
========================

Detects entities (asteroids, ...) via camera raycast and displays them on configurable screens.

------------------------------------------
CONFIGURATION
------------------------------------------

Edit the top of the script to set the operating mode:

  Mode = "Ship"       - Detects entities, maintains a local database.
                        Can synchronize with a nearby Server.
  Mode = "Server"     - Receives databases from ships, stores and
                        merges data. Does not detect on its own.
  Mode = "ServerShip" - Both detects and acts as a server.

------------------------------------------
BLOCK NAMING - Tag [SM]
------------------------------------------

Add the [SM] tag to any block you want SpaceMap to control.

  Camera:
    Any camera named with [SM] will be used for raycasting.
    Example: "Camera [SM]"

  Displays (LCD, cockpit screens, etc.):
    Append [SM] to use default mode assignment, or [SM:<mode>]
    to pick a specific screen layout.

    Available modes:
      General   - Overview list of all detected entities with
                  distance and detection age.
      Map       - 2D top-down radar circle. Objects are projected
                  onto the ship's horizontal plane. Depth (up/down)
                  is shown via a positional offset (isometric hint).
      Map3D     - 3D perspective view. The horizontal plane appears
                  as a squished ellipse. Each object is connected to
                  its position on the plane by a dashed vertical line,
                  showing its altitude relative to the ship.
      Database  - Full entry list: name, distance, detection age.
      Detection - Live raycast info: current target, range, charge.
      Help      - Quick reference of all available commands.

    Single-surface blocks (basic LCD):
      [SM]            -> General (default)
      [SM:Map]        -> Map mode
      [SM:Map3D]      -> 3D Map mode
      [SM:Database]   -> Database mode
      [SM:Detection]  -> Detection mode
      [SM:Help]       -> Help mode

    Multi-surface blocks (cockpits, terminals, ...):
      [SM]            -> Surface 0 = General, 1 = Map, 2 = Database
      [SM:Auto]       -> Same as above
      [SM:0-Map3D;1-Detection]
                      -> Surface 0 = Map3D, surface 1 = Detection
                         (any surface index, any mode, separated by ;)

------------------------------------------
COMMANDS
------------------------------------------

Run commands via the programmable block terminal argument field,
or from a button/timer block set to "Run with argument".
Use a screen tagged [SM:Help] for the in-game command reference.

  map_scale <meters>                    Alias: ms
    Set the radar display radius (Map and Map3D views).
    Example: map_scale 5000

  detect_range <meters|+delta|-delta>   Alias: dr
    Set or adjust the camera detection range.
    Example: detect_range 8000 | detect_range +2000 | dr -1000

  entry_rename <identifier> <newName>   Alias: ren
    Assign a custom name to a map entry.
    <identifier> can be:
      detected (or d) - the entity currently in the detection crosshair
      <id>            - entity ID (shown in Database mode)
      <name>          - base name (e.g. AXK-42) or current custom name
    Example: entry_rename detected "Gold Mine"
    Example: ren AXK-42 "Gold Mine"
    Example: ren 123456789 "Iron Rock"

  db_scroll (up|down|<n>)               Alias: dbs
    Scroll the database list view. up/down moves by 5 entries.
    Example: db_scroll down | dbs up | dbs -3

  db_sort <mode>                        Alias: dbso
    Sort the database list. Modes: distance, name, age, new
    Example: db_sort name | dbso distance

  disp_next [mode]                      Alias: dn
    Cycle the display mode on screens tagged [SM:Cycle],
    or jump to a specific mode.
    Modes: General, Map, Map3D, Database, Detection
    Example: disp_next | dn Map3D

------------------------------------------
DETECTION AGE
------------------------------------------

Entries are timestamped at each detection. Displays show:
  [!]  - Detected less than 60 seconds ago (new entry)
  2m   - Last seen 2 minutes ago
  1h   - Last seen 1 hour ago
  ?    - Detection time unknown (legacy entry)
